Fillets: a rounding that vanishes at its spine's end vertex, where its
faces come tangent, ends in a point there where its walk stopped short of
the vertex on the spine's own edge (mitcad#343).

The case: a bar's outline rounded with 0.3 along an edge between the bar's
side plane and an earlier concave rounding; at the edge's end vertex V the
earlier rounding goes on tangentially into a corner rounding tangent to the
side plane, so that the edge's two faces come tangent at V and the blend
vanishes there (V a tangency extremity of the spine). The stored faces
meet only within the edge's tolerance (1.5e-3): a gap g between faces at
an angle a moves the line where they meet sideways by g / a, and the ball's
contacts, R a / 2 from that line, reach the edge itself where
a^2 = 2 g / R. There the walk's contact on the earlier rounding met the
spine's own edge 0.04 short of V (the section 0.011 wide) and the walk
ended; the end was not taken as vanishing (that takes contacts within a
hundredth of the radius of V), so the corner went to the intersection at
the end, whose plate failed. The bodies stored in the files end the blend
in a point at V.

- ChFi3d_ContactOnOwnEdgeAtEnd (new): the end of a stripe whose contact
  lies on the spine's own edge E into V (an edge of the spine between the
  blend's two faces), its section no wider than sqrt(2 R tol(E)), both
  contacts within the radius of V.
- PerformFilletOnVertex: for a lone stripe ending at a tangency extremity
  where that holds, ChFi3d_ShrinkVanishingEnd puts the end at V without
  comparing the faces' normals (they are tangent at V; the walk only could
  not get nearer). The blend left between the stop and V is narrower than
  the last section, however long.
- ChFi3d_ShrinkVanishingEnd, theBendSurface (new, for those ends): the
  blend's B-spline surface is cut by a full knot at the same parameter as
  its contact curves (their boundary isos) and its end row of poles put at
  V, so that the surface ends in V with the curves; the curves' and the
  end's tolerances are their sampled deviation from the surface and from
  their faces, not the distance the end moved (which a check of the
  vertices' tolerances took for a corner left open).

On the design's stored body before the item (22 edges, four such ends):
valid, the file's 174 faces, every face on the stored body's after the item
within 0.004 mm both ways; before, one corner failed and each tangent chain
alone gave an invalid shape. Synthetic: a tower's corner (radius 0.4) and
foot (radius 3) rounded on a slab flush with its side; the side's edge with
the foot's torus rounded with 0.3 up to the vertex where all three are
tangent, the torus moved 0.0002 to 0.001 off the side within its edges'
tolerance: valid, the blend ending in a point there, the material taken
within 0.5 % of the exact body's; before, the fillet failed.

Upstream: new.
